Id: boot013e
Severity: ERROR
Category: boot
Check: check_secureboot

The system booted with UEFI, but the firmware's variables could not be
read, so whether Secure Boot is on is unknown. They are read from
efivarfs, mounted at /sys/firmware/efi/efivars; systemd mounts it at
boot ('mount -t efivarfs efivarfs /sys/firmware/efi/efivars' does it by
hand). 'mokutil --sb-state' gives the answer another way. The od
command is needed to read them.
